  "about": "CSV import and export, shared by CaveKit (CSVVectorTests.swift) and the Kotlin core (CsvVectorTest.kt). Dates are days in the device's time zone, which the tests use for both import and comparison; 'now' is the import's own date. Prices are compared as numbers. Omitted bottle and wine fields are empty. An import with a 'zone' imports and compares in that time zone; 'racks' exist in the cellar before the import (and before reading the export back); 'encoded' is the file's bytes (base64), which decode to the csv lines. 'prices' are read the same in Encave's own columns and in other files: from the first digit to the last, more than 0 and at most 100000. A rating 'x/y' is that share of 5 stars.",
